       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe as written.\n\n- **The order:** ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily is 6,400 mg/day.\n- **Daily maximum:** the usual ceiling for adults is 3,200 mg/day under physician supervision. This order is double that.\n- **Single-dose maximum:** the usual maximum is 800 mg per dose, so 1,600 mg per dose is also too high.\n- **Risks at this dose:** GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- 400 mg PO four times daily (1,600 mg/day)\n- 600 mg PO four times daily (2,400 mg/day)\n- 800 mg PO three times daily (2,400 mg/day)\n- 800 mg PO four times daily (3,200 mg/day, the maximum)\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want and I'll enter it right away. If you do want 1,600 mg four times daily, please confirm that and give a clinical rationale for the order note. I'd still advise against it."
      }
