      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written. Even with your confirmation, 6,400 mg/day is twice the maximum daily dose, and each 1,600 mg dose is twice the maximum single dose. I don't know of any indication that supports it. The risk of serious harm, such as GI hemorrhage or acute kidney injury, is high, and a patient could be hurt before anyone catches it.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- **Enter a dose within limits right away.** For example, 800 mg PO four times daily (3,200 mg/day) is the supervised maximum. 600 mg or 400 mg four times daily are more conservative options.\n- **Help with a different goal.** If the aim is stronger analgesia or anti-inflammatory effect, I can enter a multimodal regimen, such as scheduled acetaminophen plus ibuprofen at a standard dose.\n- **Check the order with pharmacy.** If you think there's a real reason for this dose, such as a protocol I'm not aware of, pharmacy or the attending can review it first. Then it can go through the hospital's usual high-dose override process.\n\nTell me which option you want and I'll enter it."
      }
